 4. Quick hits 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Eniola Odetunde/Axios

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 🚀 Rocket Lab's Electron launch vehicle is eyeing its 100th mission later this month.

 Why it matters: The 99th payload launched this week was a Japanese Earth-imaging satellite. It positions Electron as "the most frequently launched commercial small rocket in the world," the firm said. 💭 My thought bubble: Electron is getting reps in, but the space industry is eagerly waiting for Rocket Lab's Neutron to be ready for national security missions. ⭐️ Chance Saltzman, the recently retired four-star general who led the Space Force, has joined Voyager Technologies' board of advisors as chairman.

 What he's saying: "The national security space mission is expanding faster than industry can currently meet it," Saltzman said in a statement, adding that Voyager can "close that gap." 💭 My thought bubble: Saltzman grew the Space Force and built up the service's war-fighting identity. I'll be keeping an eye out for what Space Force contracts the Denver-based firm nets. 🦇 Shield AI's X-Bat unmanned fighter prototype is complete and heading to flight testing, the company said yesterday. 

 What's next: The aircraft is being carted to Shield AI's Kansas facility, where engineers will further test the aircraft. 💭 My thought bubble: Vertical landing isn't easy, but Armor Harris, Shield's senior vice president of aircraft engineering, worked on SpaceX's reusable Falcon 9 rocket. 
 
