 5. ICYMI: MAGA moonshot 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 President Trump speaks at the White House yesterday. Photo: Brendan Smialowski/AFP via Getty Images

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 So ... about that election night space proclamation. 

 President Donald Trump issued a sweeping declaration on Tuesday evening saying that outer space was "open to exploration, development, use, and the establishment of a permanent presence by American citizens." Why it matters: The White House wants to declare itself the top driver in the space race as NASA eyes an ambitious 2028 lunar return mission. 

 China is in the rearview mirror and has plans for a manned mission " before 2030 ." What they're saying: Space experts told me they were puzzled by the election night message.

 "What's unique about the declaration is the discussion of establishing settlements and a permanent presence on other celestial bodies," Aaron Brynildson, a space law instructor at the University of Mississippi, told me. That would violate the Outer Space Treaty of 1967, but Brynildson added the edict is "worded in such a way to leave enough room for an interpretation that it doesn't." "I think he wants to push the boundary without pushing the boundary," Doug Loverro, a former top NASA and Pentagon space policy official, told me. Read more here . 

 
 
