 6. Check this out 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Space Force Col. Ellen Ellis (left) and Ross Elder (right) during a simulated Mars spacewalk. Photo: Courtesy/NASA

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Cue " Life on Mars? " by David Bowie.

 Space Force Col. Ellen Ellis was one of four crew members who spent more than a year in isolation at NASA's Johnson Space Center in Houston for a mock Red Planet mission. The NASA crew entered their 1,700-square-foot, 3D-printed home away from home on Oct. 19, 2025. They exited last week, on Oct. 31. Why it matters: The White House is pushing for a manned Mars mission. These experiments are testing the limitations.

 What she's saying: "For me, maintaining American preeminence in space isn't guaranteed, but it is a national imperative, and it takes hard work," Ellis told Space Force Guardians last month .

 
 
